  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "According to bent rule more electronegative atom occupy less s-character so bond length increases. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> bond will be short than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> bond due to small size of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>. Correspondingly,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;bond in hydrogen peroxide will be shorter than that of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. Corresponding structures are:<br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c2ab2c9b-5f84-44c3-8249-b441bd80c491-26.PNG\" style=\"width: 273px; height: 282px;\" />",
    "image": null
